(517274, 50829, 259, '<td valign="top">two things could really improve your shot.  the first is to improve the lighting.  the lighting is very harsh on the bottle and blows out much of the detail on the left side.  second, i would get closer to the bottle and pick something interesting from the bottle to focus on, as well as crop tighter so as to not have so much empty meaningless space.  a different or unusual angle would also help create a more interesting subject.  shooting the whole bottle standing like you would normally see it is not very interesting and is more everyday looking.</td>', 'two things could really improve your shot.  the first is to improve the lighting.  the lighting is very harsh on the bottle and blows out much of the detail on the left side.  second, i would get closer to the bottle and pick something interesting from the bottle to focus on, as well as crop tighter so as to not have so much empty meaningless space.  a different or unusual angle would also help create a more interesting subject.  shooting the whole bottle standing like you would normally see it is not very interesting and is more everyday looking.', '2003-12-18 22:51:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(517276, 50561, 14012, '<td valign="top">For a minute there I thought you attempted to recreate a shot similar to kiwi''s previous ribbon winner, but then I realized how you did this. Nice capture and 180 degree rotation to change it up a little. 8 for now</td>', 'For a minute there I thought you attempted to recreate a shot similar to kiwi''s previous ribbon winner, but then I realized how you did this. Nice capture and 180 degree rotation to change it up a little. 8 for now', '2003-12-18 22:55:12.000000', NULL, 1),
