(521315, 50673, 15291, '<td valign="top">Steve,<br/>    The B&amp;W works well here. But from a compositional stand point it could have been vastly improved by simply having the young lady turn her head more to the camera. If you look at her head you have very nice detail along the hair line, her browe &amp; eye lashes. The water on her face shows very nice detail also. As we move to the right however you begin to lose all detail of the hair to the point that it is a black blouch. You also begin to lose detail in the water the futher down and right you go the worse it gets to a point that it looks like your lense is dirty ( see the white spotting pattern of the water ). By turning her head more to the camera this problem could have been avoided. The water, slowing down the shutter speed would have given the water a sence of motion giving the photo a sence of life. This photo looks a little flat because of the (freeze frame) stopping the water. The piece of teflon tape on the shower head is a bit distracting also. If possible try shooting that same shot giving the water a sence of motion and using the strong details of the eyes,browse, and hair line and you will see a huge difference.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Steve,    The B&W works well here. But from a compositional stand point it could have been vastly improved by simply having the young lady turn her head more to the camera. If you look at her head you have very nice detail along the hair line, her browe & eye lashes. The water on her face shows very nice detail also. As we move to the right however you begin to lose all detail of the hair to the point that it is a black blouch. You also begin to lose detail in the water the futher down and right you go the worse it gets to a point that it looks like your lense is dirty ( see the white spotting pattern of the water ). By turning her head more to the camera this problem could have been avoided. The water, slowing down the shutter speed would have given the water a sence of motion giving the photo a sence of life. This photo looks a little flat because of the (freeze frame) stopping the water. The piece of teflon tape on the shower head is a bit distracting also. If possible try shooting that same shot giving the water a sence of motion and using the strong details of the eyes,browse, and hair line and you will see a huge difference. ', '2003-12-23 21:02:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(521380, 50848, 10702, '<td valign="top">Skil ekki hvernig þessi mynd gat mögulega lent svona neðarlega. Hún er algjör snilld. Að hún fái bara tvær níur og tvær tíur en svo afturámóti fjóra tvista og fimm þrista er algjört bull. Hefði allavega átt að lenda í top 10, þetta er mjög vel gert.</td>', 'Skil ekki hvernig þessi mynd gat mögulega lent svona neðarlega. Hún er algjör snilld. Að hún fái bara tvær níur og tvær tíur en svo afturámóti fjóra tvista og fimm þrista er algjört bull. Hefði allavega átt að lenda í top 10, þetta er mjög vel gert.', '2003-12-23 22:23:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(522154, 50886, 10402, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>You''ve achieved a nice effect here. The transition from clear to red is perfect, and the frozen drops add impact. The drops on the inside of the glass are a bit distracting, but unavoidable. The composition works well; the space on the left opens up the image, suggesting the libation will be offered to someone after it is poured. The glare on the left of the glass is near the edge so helps define the contour without getting in the way. The glare on the right isn''t quite so useful; a small specular highlight (like the one to the left of the water stream) would have been preferable. But overall a great photo.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! You''ve achieved a nice effect here. The transition from clear to red is perfect, and the frozen drops add impact. The drops on the inside of the glass are a bit distracting, but unavoidable. The composition works well; the space on the left opens up the image, suggesting the libation will be offered to someone after it is poured. The glare on the left of the glass is near the edge so helps define the contour without getting in the way. The glare on the right isn''t quite so useful; a small specular highlight (like the one to the left of the water stream) would have been preferable. But overall a great photo.', '2003-12-24 11:59:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(522193, 50660, 5792, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on another well deserved #1!<br/> <br/>I like the steps you took to produce this outstanding final image. Those are now registered in the back of my mind, especially the layer manipulation to enhance the image in different ways. Removing halos is a must.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-12-24 12:19:46.</i></td>', 'Congratulations on another well deserved #1! I like the steps you took to produce this outstanding final image. Those are now registered in the back of my mind, especially the layer manipulation to enhance the image in different ways. Removing halos is a must.', '2003-12-24 12:19:15.000000', '2003-12-24 12:19:46.000000', 0),
(522196, 50852, 5792, '<td valign="top">Congratulations and outstanding work. <br/> <br/>Intellisharpen must be a good tool given this result.</td>', 'Congratulations and outstanding work.  Intellisharpen must be a good tool given this result.', '2003-12-24 12:22:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(522197, 50872, 11737, '<td valign="top">Góóóóður, vissi alltaf að þú gætir þetta, til hamingju og gleðileg jól</td>', 'Góóóóður, vissi alltaf að þú gætir þetta, til hamingju og gleðileg jól', '2003-12-24 12:22:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(522198, 50611, 5792, '<td valign="top">This is a great shot and you did not use any of the December Rules.</td>', 'This is a great shot and you did not use any of the December Rules.', '2003-12-24 12:23:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(522204, 50087, 5792, '<td valign="top">This is an outstanding image, particularly since you did not apply any of the "December Rules". The long exposure time and good color makes this image special.<br/> <br/>You have a hot spot in the lower center left. You might carefully select around it with the lasso or select it with the Magic Wand (in PS) to tone down the spot.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-12-24 12:29:13.</i></td>', 'This is an outstanding image, particularly since you did not apply any of the "December Rules". The long exposure time and good color makes this image special. You have a hot spot in the lower center left. You might carefully select around it with the lasso or select it with the Magic Wand (in PS) to tone down the spot.', '2003-12-24 12:27:10.000000', '2003-12-24 12:29:13.000000', 0),
(522238, 50087, 8125, '<td valign="top">Thank you for the great comments everyone.  I''m very happy with 5th place.  <br/> <br/>Steve, thanks a lot for the tip on the hot spot.  I ended up using the dodge/burn tool for the print and I think it came out better that way.</td>', 'Thank you for the great comments everyone.  I''m very happy with 5th place.   Steve, thanks a lot for the tip on the hot spot.  I ended up using the dodge/burn tool for the print and I think it came out better that way.', '2003-12-24 12:53:17.000000', NULL, 0),
