(523648, 50816, 10420, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone. I am kind of proud of this photo, cause I outscored my mom again :-))</td>', 'Thanks everyone. I am kind of proud of this photo, cause I outscored my mom again :-))', '2003-12-27 04:24:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(523743, 50496, 10402, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>This image successfully conveys the essence of Chinese water torture. The creative choices work well: The light blue color gives the impression of cold and pain a lot more than either normal skin tones or gray would have. The foreboding black background gives an air of malice; about twice as much would have had more impact. Showing the splash is visually more attractive than a drop about to hit and conveys a greater sense of torture. The lighting works well, especially the use of flash to freeze the motion of the water drop. And as you mentioned in your comments, the eye is a necessary reference point so the viewer can tell it''s a forehead, although I think cropping the bottom half would have improved the photo. The technical quality is high (including the spot editing).<br/> <br/>Overall, this is not an attractive photo, but one that does convey a specific idea very well. (And perhaps it also explains why your profile photo shows you touching your forehead. Does your girlfriend do this to you often?)</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! This image successfully conveys the essence of Chinese water torture. The creative choices work well: The light blue color gives the impression of cold and pain a lot more than either normal skin tones or gray would have. The foreboding black background gives an air of malice; about twice as much would have had more impact. Showing the splash is visually more attractive than a drop about to hit and conveys a greater sense of torture. The lighting works well, especially the use of flash to freeze the motion of the water drop. And as you mentioned in your comments, the eye is a necessary reference point so the viewer can tell it''s a forehead, although I think cropping the bottom half would have improved the photo. The technical quality is high (including the spot editing). Overall, this is not an attractive photo, but one that does convey a specific idea very well. (And perhaps it also explains why your profile photo shows you touching your forehead. Does your girlfriend do this to you often?)', '2003-12-27 10:57:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(523849, 50849, 7969, '<td valign="top">Hi greetings from the critique club, here goes my thoughts and ideas on your shot. First of all,  I love the dew drops!!  I think your subject is a little too central and would benefit from being shifted a little to the right, I also think if it was cropped a bit more tightly it would help to highlight the actual subject and cut out the frivilous leaves on ground.  I also wonder if there would be a way to get the Sundew to be a little darker, or perhaps a bit might contrast may make it ''pop'' out a little more.  You obviously have a great eye to find such a beautiful and small subject to shoot, which is great!!  Another suggestion may have been to bend that leaf that overlaps the flower out of the way as you took the shot, leaving your subject unobstructed.  Keep up the good work noticing the details and interesting subjects around!!<br/>Good work!</td>', 'Hi greetings from the critique club, here goes my thoughts and ideas on your shot. First of all,  I love the dew drops!!  I think your subject is a little too central and would benefit from being shifted a little to the right, I also think if it was cropped a bit more tightly it would help to highlight the actual subject and cut out the frivilous leaves on ground.  I also wonder if there would be a way to get the Sundew to be a little darker, or perhaps a bit might contrast may make it ''pop'' out a little more.  You obviously have a great eye to find such a beautiful and small subject to shoot, which is great!!  Another suggestion may have been to bend that leaf that overlaps the flower out of the way as you took the shot, leaving your subject unobstructed.  Keep up the good work noticing the details and interesting subjects around!!Good work!', '2003-12-27 12:38:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(523860, 50728, 7969, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the CC, here goes my suggestions, please take them as that and not more :  ).  I like the idea of your subject, and i really like the way the light is in the outer rings,  I think the rust helps to add a real warmth in color (though it worries me you drink it  : (  ).    I  do find the concrete wall to be a little distracting and such a stark contrast to the light and movemnt  of the water.  I would be curious to see the walls of the sink cropped out. I think the composition of the drain in the corner works very well.  I also like that the water is running and adds an additional point of interest.  I think your photo makes a good point about water more than wows so to speak, but I think there is certainly a place for this kind of photography! Keep up the work!</td>', 'Greetings from the CC, here goes my suggestions, please take them as that and not more :  ).  I like the idea of your subject, and i really like the way the light is in the outer rings,  I think the rust helps to add a real warmth in color (though it worries me you drink it  : (  ).    I  do find the concrete wall to be a little distracting and such a stark contrast to the light and movemnt  of the water.  I would be curious to see the walls of the sink cropped out. I think the composition of the drain in the corner works very well.  I also like that the water is running and adds an additional point of interest.  I think your photo makes a good point about water more than wows so to speak, but I think there is certainly a place for this kind of photography! Keep up the work!', '2003-12-27 12:49:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(523933, 50813, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hi Rc,<br/>    It''s all there as far as I am concearned. A very technically sound photo. All of the elements I look for in a photo have a very strong presents. I like your use of the curved peninsula as your leading lines taking you in and out of the photo. The fisherman &amp; dog are well placed giving the photo a sense of scale.The curve in the banks give the photo life.The back drop of water &amp; bushes give the photo a great sense depth.The reflection of the bushes give the photo a intimate aspect as a private relaxing fishing hole (excellent). The ripples on the water bring life to the entire area giving the viewer a sense of truely being outdoors. The color &amp; detail though out the photo are well done. The photographs over all composition is fantastic. There are 4 minor problems I see here. 1) the bush left of center next to the rocks is a little blown out.2) The rocks leading up the hill in the back ground are also blown out a bit.3) the water to the left of dad there is a tweek hot.4)The red spot to the right by the shadow line. It is probably the bobber attached to the fishing line but it stands out to much. A polarizing filter I beleave would have corrected these very minor problems. Over all this is a fantasic image know dout taken from a very talented photographer. It was well thought out and every consideration was given to all it''s elements. The photograph tells us a complete story not part or half it''s all there. A job well done all the way around Rc.</td>', 'Hi Rc,    It''s all there as far as I am concearned. A very technically sound photo. All of the elements I look for in a photo have a very strong presents. I like your use of the curved peninsula as your leading lines taking you in and out of the photo. The fisherman & dog are well placed giving the photo a sense of scale.The curve in the banks give the photo life.The back drop of water & bushes give the photo a great sense depth.The reflection of the bushes give the photo a intimate aspect as a private relaxing fishing hole (excellent). The ripples on the water bring life to the entire area giving the viewer a sense of truely being outdoors. The color & detail though out the photo are well done. The photographs over all composition is fantastic. There are 4 minor problems I see here. 1) the bush left of center next to the rocks is a little blown out.2) The rocks leading up the hill in the back ground are also blown out a bit.3) the water to the left of dad there is a tweek hot.4)The red spot to the right by the shadow line. It is probably the bobber attached to the fishing line but it stands out to much. A polarizing filter I beleave would have corrected these very minor problems. Over all this is a fantasic image know dout taken from a very talented photographer. It was well thought out and every consideration was given to all it''s elements. The photograph tells us a complete story not part or half it''s all there. A job well done all the way around Rc.', '2003-12-27 15:05:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(524126, 50901, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>This photo definitely meets the challenge with no problems.  The water is the dominant theme in the image.<br/> <br/>I can''t really put my finger on what it is about this photo that makes me struggle though.  It may be the composition.  It may also be the background color.  The brown in the background doesn''t seem to complement the color of the flowers in any way.  This could have been a good opportunity to consider the benefits of primary/secondary color combinations and how they work together to produce pleasing images.  <br/> <br/>I think the composition may seem uncomfortable because it is horizontal.  The water spray is flowing along the short direction.  If this composition was vertical, the flow of water through the scene could possibly be more appealing :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) This photo definitely meets the challenge with no problems.  The water is the dominant theme in the image. I can''t really put my finger on what it is about this photo that makes me struggle though.  It may be the composition.  It may also be the background color.  The brown in the background doesn''t seem to complement the color of the flowers in any way.  This could have been a good opportunity to consider the benefits of primary/secondary color combinations and how they work together to produce pleasing images.   I think the composition may seem uncomfortable because it is horizontal.  The water spray is flowing along the short direction.  If this composition was vertical, the flow of water through the scene could possibly be more appealing :) John Setzler', '2003-12-27 21:10:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(524399, 50829, 6624, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club:<br/> <br/>This was an interesting and challenging image that you set for yourself.  Overall the image seems lifeless and the soft focus underscores that rather than enticing the viewer into the image.  Perhaps you might have thought of a different angle, maybe something additional to the water to add interest, or just moving in on the bottle and choosing something in the lable to focus on in order to add clarity about your intent.  As the image is it lacks any real impact and the background and shadow are dull and flat.  It also appears that the image/bottle is tilted and that, too, is a distraction. Another approach to correcting this would have been different lighting, coming from a different angle and diffused a bit to keep the softness but add a little zing. Thanks for the image.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club: This was an interesting and challenging image that you set for yourself.  Overall the image seems lifeless and the soft focus underscores that rather than enticing the viewer into the image.  Perhaps you might have thought of a different angle, maybe something additional to the water to add interest, or just moving in on the bottle and choosing something in the lable to focus on in order to add clarity about your intent.  As the image is it lacks any real impact and the background and shadow are dull and flat.  It also appears that the image/bottle is tilted and that, too, is a distraction. Another approach to correcting this would have been different lighting, coming from a different angle and diffused a bit to keep the softness but add a little zing. Thanks for the image.', '2003-12-28 11:37:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(524417, 50428, 9906, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club<br/> <br/>This is a nice shot for the challenge.  I don''t recall seeing any others close to this subject which gets a bonus from me for originality!<br/> <br/>This shot is framed and composed nicely!  I like the angular lines infered by the boy and the penguin looking at each other!  From a compositional POV there is an object (another penguin?) in the background on the right that is a little distracting.  I don''t know with all the patterns in the water if you could clone this out or not...  There is a bit of noise here, but I don''t think it really detracts from the shot.  I''m not sure that I like the choice of B/W for this though.  I am a color freak and in this shot I think that the colors and tones from the light coming through the water would add to the feeling of the shot!<br/> <br/>Nice shot overall.<br/>TC</td>', 'From the Critique Club This is a nice shot for the challenge.  I don''t recall seeing any others close to this subject which gets a bonus from me for originality! This shot is framed and composed nicely!  I like the angular lines infered by the boy and the penguin looking at each other!  From a compositional POV there is an object (another penguin?) in the background on the right that is a little distracting.  I don''t know with all the patterns in the water if you could clone this out or not...  There is a bit of noise here, but I don''t think it really detracts from the shot.  I''m not sure that I like the choice of B/W for this though.  I am a color freak and in this shot I think that the colors and tones from the light coming through the water would add to the feeling of the shot! Nice shot overall.TC', '2003-12-28 13:17:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(524744, 50884, 12448, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Hi!  I really like this shot but then again anything with an animal automatically gets extra points from me, LOL!<br/> <br/>You are right in that you probably lost points for not having the water as the main focus but the clarity on the duck is amazing and the overall DOF works very well for this shot.  I like the cropping on the right side, you are brought into the shot by either corner, the tree in the upper corner, the duck''s neck in the lower corner.  The left side leaves me a bit disoriented though.  I put my hand up trying to see what might make it work a little better for me and I''m thinking just a little tighter crop, either so the tree borders the left side or crop right inside the tree so the water is all on the left seems a bit more composed to me.<br/> <br/>The lighting and shadows on this shot are wonderful, I love sunlight shots too.  <br/> <br/>Hope this helps!<br/> <br/>Good Luck In Future Challenges!<br/> <br/>Deannda<br/>DNeufer@stny.rr.com if you have any questions or want to discuss this further!</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Hi!  I really like this shot but then again anything with an animal automatically gets extra points from me, LOL! You are right in that you probably lost points for not having the water as the main focus but the clarity on the duck is amazing and the overall DOF works very well for this shot.  I like the cropping on the right side, you are brought into the shot by either corner, the tree in the upper corner, the duck''s neck in the lower corner.  The left side leaves me a bit disoriented though.  I put my hand up trying to see what might make it work a little better for me and I''m thinking just a little tighter crop, either so the tree borders the left side or crop right inside the tree so the water is all on the left seems a bit more composed to me. The lighting and shadows on this shot are wonderful, I love sunlight shots too.   Hope this helps! Good Luck In Future Challenges! DeanndaDNeufer@stny.rr.com if you have any questions or want to discuss this further!', '2003-12-28 22:32:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(529970, 50818, 2178, '<td valign="top">Great color, love staring into this.</td>', 'Great color, love staring into this.', '2004-01-02 19:10:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(537978, 50746, 15703, '<td valign="top">An absolutely beautiful choice of location for a flowing water shot.  I think this exposure is spot-on - a longer exposure would have robbed us of that dynamic gushing of the water. A very minor negative -  I find the thick, dark border unpleasant -  enclosing and claustrophobic. But the photo is excellent.</td>', 'An absolutely beautiful choice of location for a flowing water shot.  I think this exposure is spot-on - a longer exposure would have robbed us of that dynamic gushing of the water. A very minor negative -  I find the thick, dark border unpleasant -  enclosing and claustrophobic. But the photo is excellent.', '2004-01-10 10:53:45.000000', NULL, 0),
