(858878, 50527, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by KarenB:</b></div><hr/><i> Paul, this is really cool too. I scored it fairly high during voting during the challenge.<br/> <br/>Just had another thought...<br/>Did you try to rotate it CW a bit, to give a bit of a slant to the composition? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks! I think I was trying to get the left edge straight, but I can see where a slight rotation clockwise would make the implied (but unseen) horizon straighter. I''ll have to see if there''s enough uncropped area to the left to try that.</td>', 'Originally posted by KarenB: Paul, this is really cool too. I scored it fairly high during voting during the challenge. Just had another thought...Did you try to rotate it CW a bit, to give a bit of a slant to the composition?  Thanks! I think I was trying to get the left edge straight, but I can see where a slight rotation clockwise would make the implied (but unseen) horizon straighter. I''ll have to see if there''s enough uncropped area to the left to try that.', '2004-08-13 17:20:52.000000', NULL, 0),
